cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "slChannel: semi-Lagrangian DNS of turbulent channel flow on GPUs"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cavallazzi
    given-names: Giorgio Maria
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7529-3256"
    affiliation: "City St. George's, University of London"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gmcavallazzi/SLchannel"
abstract: >-
  A GPU direct-numerical-simulation solver for incompressible turbulent channel
  flow that replaces CFL-limited explicit advection with unconditionally stable
  second-order semi-Lagrangian advection along characteristics (Boukir et al.
  1997, BDF2). The timestep is then limited by physical accuracy rather than by
  an advective CFL condition, giving a 2.65x reduction in wall-clock time per
  simulated time unit at matched turbulence statistics.
references:
  - type: data
    title: "seed field SLchannel Re_tau = 180"
    authors:
      - family-names: Cavallazzi
        given-names: Giorgio Maria
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7529-3256"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22099568
    year: 2026
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - direct numerical simulation
  - semi-Lagrangian advection
  - turbulent channel flow
  - GPU
  - PyTorch
